# Generated benchmark instances. Not committed: they are reproducible byte for
# byte from instance-generator/ plus the Solomon sources in cuOpt/testcases/,
# and they get large fast (1k = 14 MB, 10k ~ 140 MB, 100k ~ 1.4 GB).
# cuOpt/instances/README.md IS committed, so the regeneration commands survive
# even though the instances themselves do not. NB: these patterns contain a
# slash, so git anchors them to this file's directory -- a bare "instances/*"
# would NOT match cuOpt/instances/.
# cuOpt/instances/*
# !cuOpt/instances/README.md

# The self-contained Paramshakti run folder. Its scripts are committed; the
# generated instances (83 MB, and regenerable) are not.
cuOpt_FSMVRPTW/instances/
cuOpt_FSMVRPTW/outputs_cuopt/*.csv

# Our solver. Source is committed; instances are regenerable, build artefacts
# and run output are not worth versioning.
FSMVRPTW_Solver/instances/
FSMVRPTW_Solver/reference/
FSMVRPTW_Solver/outputs/
FSMVRPTW_Solver/solve_cvrptw
FSMVRPTW_Solver/**/*.o
FSMVRPTW_Solver/**/*.d
FSMVRPTW_Solver/.build_mode

# Scratch from the smoke test, and SLURM job logs.
# cuOpt/smoke_in/
# cuOpt/smoke_routes/
# cuOpt/*.out
# cuOpt/*.err

# NOTE: cuOpt/outputs_cuopt/*.csv is deliberately NOT ignored. Result sheets are
# small and are the one thing here that cannot be regenerated -- they depend on
# the GPU and on wall-clock timing -- so they belong in version control.

# Text dumps extracted from PDFs while reading them. Scratch, regenerate as needed.
Papers/_*.txt
paramshakthi/manual.txt

__pycache__/
*.pyc


Background_Material/

Papers/
paramshakthi/
Dinesh-Code-Base/
Sneh-Code-Base/
Results/
Algorithm-Ideas.md
MTP-Notes.md
cuOpt/

cuOpt-Baseline-Findings.md
Dinesh-Code-Base.zip
Solver-Port-Plan.md

.claude/*.json
.claude/